// Stop trying to build a central omniscient engine; channel teams will bypass it.
// Treat customer attention as scarce inventory with an internal shadow price.
function arbitrate_touchpoint(customer_id, incoming_event):
  state = get_attention_state(customer_id) // Tracks recent fatigue and current service state, not full history
  if state.has_open_high_severity_service_case():
    return suppress_marketing() // Obvious answer is prioritize sales; reality is care always overrides growth
  // Let channels bid their own perceived upside; don't try to centrally predict creative nuance
  bids = [ch.propose_action(state) for ch in registered_channels]
  // Penalize bids using a global fatigue tax rather than naive hard frequency caps
  scored = [b.expected_value - state.channel_shadow_price(b.channel) for b in bids]
  winner = max(scored, key=lambda x: x.net_value)
  // Default to silence: the risk-adjusted value of doing nothing is routinely underestimated
  if winner.net_value <= 0:
    return suppress_all()
  grant_channel_lease(winner.channel, lease_duration="15m") // Return short lease; don't orchestrate execution
  state.inflate_shadow_price(winner.fatigue_cost) // Immediately increment cost locally to kill race conditions

Don’t build one brain to rule each glowing screen;
Choose one small journey, map the state between.
Log every touch and cost, hold groups aside;
In shadow mode, compare the channel tide.
Let margin, fatigue, and service each have sway;
No single score can wish their trade-offs away.
Late signals, guarded budgets bar the door;
We may prove narrow gains—the whole stays unsure.
